    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are staring down a slate where our primary value is being driven by favorable matchups against soft pitching rotations rather than top-tier offensive output. **Nasim Nunez** (64.14) is our strongest play today; his matchup against Ryan Feltner is a goldmine for an Ottoneu roster prioritizing stolen base upside. The combination of an elite 5.10 xERA opponent and Nunez\u2019s projected spot in the lineup makes him the essential anchor for our stolen base target. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (59.34) benefits significantly from his leadoff role against Kumar Rocker; his +10% boost for hitting at the top of the order elevates his floor, making him a mandatory start in our MI slot as we look to maximize our R and SB volume.\n\nOur decision-making process was complicated by the daily efficiency requirements, specifically regarding **Liam Hicks** (49.04) and **Tommy White** (55.05). While **Liam Hicks** carries a sub-50 score due to the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Framber Valdez, he remains the most viable option given our current roster constraints. Conversely, **Tommy White** serves as a solid mid-range start, benefiting from a favorable +10% park factor that offsets the middling skill profile of Zebby Matthews. The most challenging bench decision involved balancing the UTIL slot between **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) and our bench depth. **Miguel Vargas** ultimately edged out the remaining reserves\u2014including players like **Heliot Ramos** and **Jordan Westburg**\u2014due to a strong 0.389 xwOBA, which suggests he is primed to outperform his base projection despite the neutral conditions against Rocker. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Liam Hicks**, as a move down the order would trigger a further reduction in efficiency. We are also navigating a quiet day for our core offensive weapons; the lack of availability for **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014all of whom have scheduled off-days\u2014means we are relying on our depth pieces like **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) to hold the line. **Jackson Merrill** is a high-risk, high-reward play today; while his -18% SP skill adjustment is concerning against Braxton Ashcraft, his +13% dynamic platoon edge provides enough leverage to keep him active in our pursuit of 5x5 category gains.",
